    "THE CONTEXT AROUND IT",
    "Rockstar has a history of heavy location research for its worlds, and the later Game Informer cover story made clear how seriously the GTA VI team studied Florida: developers discussed beaches, nightlife, the Keys, the Everglades and other real-world reference work. That later context does not retroactively authenticate every 2019 claim, but it explains why the scouting story felt plausible.",
    "WHY IT MATTERED",
    "The clue mattered because it shifted speculation from pure wish-list thinking toward something that resembled production evidence. For years, “Vice City” was the answer many fans wanted; the scouting report made it feel possible that the studio itself was collecting the visual vocabulary needed to build a modern Florida parody. That helped sustain the setting theory long before Rockstar showed a palm tree or skyline.",
    "WHAT NOT TO OVERREAD",
    "At the time, the connection remained unconfirmed. A location request can support research without proving the final setting, era, map boundaries or project identity. Any reconstruction of 2019 should preserve that uncertainty rather than rewriting the rumor as an official teaser simply because Leonida later turned out to be Florida-inspired.",
