    "THE CONTEXT AROUND IT",
    "Those details mattered because GTA VI had already proven it could look spectacular. The remaining question was depth: what makes a long drive, a swamp, a shoreline or a storm feel different after dozens of hours? Wildlife and weather are systemic answers to that question. They can alter atmosphere without requiring a mission marker, making the environment itself part of the player’s memory.",
    "WHY IT MATTERED",
