    "The pre-load milestone is less glamorous than a trailer, but it may be the moment the wait feels most real. The icon is on the system, the files are present, and the calendar has only one week left. Everything after that is measured in days and hours rather than years.",
    "WHAT FANS WERE WATCHING FOR",
    "The community response centered on the calendar. Once a date or window enters the public record, every later piece of news is interpreted relative to it: marketing frequency, store updates, ratings, press access and platform activity all start to look like signals. Some of those signals are useful, others are noise. The cleanest historical approach is to keep the official date beside the date it replaced and let later milestones show whether confidence strengthened or weakened.",
